Depends: paladin-seeker (>= 1.8.0), paladin-dock, python3, python3-gi, x11-utils, x11-xserver-utils, dbus-user-session, xsettingsd, lightdm, util-linux, appmenu-gtk3-module, python3-xlib, python3-pil, fonts-noto-core, palos-screenshot, paladin-save-sheets
Recommends: paladin-settings, paladin-login, paladin-boot, palos-icons, openbox, brightnessctl, playerctl, pipewire-bin | pulseaudio-utils, libnotify-bin
Description: Paladin desktop session: steel title bars, GTK theme, cursor and tools
 A login session that replaces GNOME Shell: Compiz with Paladin title bars,
 Seeker (desktop, menu bar, file browser) and Paladin Dock, plus the helpers a
 desktop needs (keyring, admin prompts, notifications, media keys, screen lock,
 screenshots, Num Lock, app settings). GNOME stays installed and selectable at
 the login screen.
 .
 Includes the Paladin look in light and dark (slate) versions: title bars with
 steel-blue window buttons, a GTK 3 theme, colors for GTK 4 / libadwaita apps,
 and the Paladin cursor. The Dark Mode switch in Paladin Settings changes all
 of them at once.
